WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.560
Let's go, Kaiba!

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.480
I flip over my set card!

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.750
Card Destruction!

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.620
What?

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.340
Card Destruction?

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.240
Tributes are required to summon high Level monsters.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:40.410
But there's a way to bring a monster to the field without tributing.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.010
My turn!

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.150
I flip over my set card!

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.880
Monster Reborn!

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:54.460
That's...

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:55.600
Kaiba!

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.250
Card Destruction sent Blue-Eyes to the graveyard, but I now revive it!

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:07.240
Unite!

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.920
Blue-Eyes White Dragon revives!

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.120
Blue-Eyes!

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.540
Kaiba, do you finally understand the meaning of teamwork?

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.400
Damn.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:29.030
I never thought they'd work together and use Card Destruction and Monster Reborn for a counter combo.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.030
Yugi and Kaiba...

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.600
They shouldn't have teamwork.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:41.770
I understand what I need to win a tag match, Yugi.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.280
Kaiba...

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:47.020
Does Kaiba finally understand teamwork?

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.280
Now we can win!

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:52.560
I need to use my partner.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:59.680
In order to bring out my high Level monster, I made you play Card Destruction.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.560
Just as I planned.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:07.730
You mistook it for your lame idea of "teamwork."

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.570
How naïve.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.880
I've paid back my debt.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:19.940
Yugi, the next time they attack you, don't expect my Blue-Eyes to save you.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:23.580
Kaiba...

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.590
They don't have any teamwork.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:31.240
Kaiba, it's your Battle Phase.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:40.480
Even though you summoned Blue-Eyes White Dragon, The Masked Beast has 3200 attack points.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:45.600
Blue-Eyes only has 3000 attack points, so it'll be destroyed if it attacks.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.240
Attack, Kaiba!

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.110
What?

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.480
Blue-Eyes can destroy The Masked Beast!

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.930
Do you believe me?

00:03:55.930 --> 00:04:00.980
Or will Blue-Eyes retreat this turn after all you've done to bring it back?

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:08.280
If I lose Blue-Eyes, we can't win.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.990
Prove your courage, Kaiba!

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.110
Interesting, Yugi.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:17.600
I never thought you'd say that to me.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.770
I won't retreat!

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.410
Blue-Eyes attacks!

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:24.500
What?

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.650
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.560
The Masked Beast is destroyed!

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.560
What?  Impossible!

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.070
I destroyed it...

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:51.910
Why?

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.570
Why was it destroyed?

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:58.420
Due to Card Destruction's effect, all cards in my hand went to the graveyard.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:03.870
Among them was a monster card whose effect activates when it's sent to the graveyard.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:11.860
When Archfiend of Gilfer goes to the graveyard, it becomes an Equip Card.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:15.510
It equips on to one monster on the field.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:22.200
The equipped monster loses 500 attack points.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:27.710
Due to that card, The Masked Beast lost 500 attack points?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:34.940
When I was reviving Blue-Eyes,Yugi already formed a plan to destroy our opponent's monster.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.180
That's why he played Card Destruction.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:42.690
Kaiba, this is the power of teamwork!

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.040
"Teamwork" is only a word.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:50.400
Yugi manipulated me.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.200
I end my turn.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.320
We have no monsters to defend with.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:06.480
If Blue-Eyes strikes us next turn, we're in trouble.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:07.980
My turn!

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.980
I set a monster in defense position.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.990
And I set two more cards and end my turn.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.990
He set cards...

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:25.120
I'll take care of Blue-Eyes with these set cards.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.000
Yugi, it's your turn!

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:37.200
Don't forget that due to Mask of the Accursed and Mask of Dispel, you lose 1000 life points.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:42.010
My turn!

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:50.860
By using Card Destruction to replace my hand, I can play a monster this turn.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.530
I set a card!

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:58.840
I summon Alpha The Magnet Warrior!

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.270
Attack!

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.740
I can't use my set card against a weakling!

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:10.880
Magnet Air Sword!

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:15.480
Melchid is destroyed!

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.720
I must remain focused on Blue-Eyes!

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:21.900
I end my turn.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:30.460
Partner, if we don't get rid of that Blue-Eyes, we'll be the ones plummeting to the earth.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.620
Don't worry, partner.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.060
I can destroy Blue-Eyes.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:39.800
Use the monster card in your hand to attack Blue-Eyes.

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:41.160
Okay.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:01.260
Is there any way to escape?

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:07.330
If I can get out, I can have Kaiba Corporation crush the Ghouls.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:12.470
You may be able to escape.

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.910
You're a Ghoul!  What are you after?

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:29.700
It's better for you if you don't know.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.420
You won't understand anyway.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:34.150
Tell me anyway!

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:38.320
I know you're after Yugi's rare cards.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:45.000
A first-rate duelist won't go easy on you just because you took me hostage.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.450
Neither will Yugi.

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:55.380
What are you going to do to me?

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.790
Hurry!  They're coming!

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.280
Okay.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:16.800
Anzu, what about you?

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:20.340
I'll be fine, so tell the others!

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:21.280
Hey!

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:21.960
Hurry!

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:22.840
Okay!

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:36.380
Anzu!

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:42.840
Don't worry about me!  Just go!

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.640
I promise to bring help!

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:48.200
How dare you!

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:50.650
Don't let the kid escape!

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.200
Mokuba, I'm counting on you.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.200
Find him?

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.200
Nothing over here.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:09:59.860
Keep searching!

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:06.220
I promise to save you, Anzu.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.390
My turn!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.050
I summon Rogue Doll!

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:23.250
It only has 1600 attack points.

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:26.000
That monster is made to lose.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.900
It's no match for my Blue-Eyes.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.910
So why is he so calm?

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.410
We'll see about that, Kaiba.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.620
Go, Rogue Doll!

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.780
Attack Blue-Eyes!

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.790
They don't know their place.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:50.590
I flip over my set card!

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:53.100
Mask of Weakness!

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:54.800
Weakness?

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:03.200
Mask of Weakness equips on to Blue-Eyes!

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:12.400
Due to Mask of Weakness's curse, Blue-Eyes loses 700 attack points.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.150
Next...

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:17.150
Mask of Brutality!

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:23.680
The monster wearing this mask gains 1000 attack points.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:32.170
Vanish, Blue-Eyes!

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:33.960
Not so fast!

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:38.860
I activate my trap!

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.620
Mystical Refpanel!

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.510
This card steals your power!

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:02.450
I activate my trap!

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.400
Mystical Refpanel!

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:08.270
This card steals your power!

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:16.180
Rogue Doll's Mask of Brutality is gone!

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.530
Mask of Brutality equips on top of Mask of Weakness!

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:25.160
Blue-Eyes regains 1000 attack points!

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.690
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:33.130
What is power?

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:36.530
Power is the only thing you can trust...

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.400
...in order to survive.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:45.320
In a battle, everyone is my enemy.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:51.710
Power is a weapon given to me to crush my enemies and protect myself.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:55.720
Power should only exist for me.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:58.720
But the power of teamwork...

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:03.730
Does the power of teamwork exceed my power?

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:06.730
My life points!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.880
Partner, are you okay?

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:14.240
I attacked because you told me to, but look what happened!

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.970
You're blaming me?

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:19.420
You didn't see this coming either!

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:19.970
Be quiet!

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:23.520
Their teamwork is falling apart.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:26.210
If we can break them up...

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:32.300
But victory will still depend on the power of our teamwork.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:35.720
My turn isn't over yet!

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:39.700
We don't have a monster to protect us.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:44.800
If Blue-Eyes attacks next turn, I'll be caught in the explosion.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.600
I won't rely on my partner anymore.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.910
I will protect myself.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.440
I set a card!

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.410
I end my turn!

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:11.740
Are you okay?

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:12.500
Yes.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:16.760
We'll arrive at Domino City in a few hours.

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:21.270
What's wrong?  Are you feeling sick?

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:23.620
No, I'm happy!

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.270
I can finally see my brother duel?

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:28.780
Yeah.  You can count on me.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:40.170
My turn!

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:42.990
Power!  Power!  Power!

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:50.460
The mighty and invincible Blue-Eyes represents my power!

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:52.970
Blue-Eyes, annihilate them!

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:54.960
Burst Stream!

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:01.070
Atack Mask of Darkness directly!

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:05.220
If this attack succeeds, Mask of Darkness will be defeated.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:08.300
But this attack is too simple!

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:11.700
A duelist as good as Kaiba should know this!

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:13.120
What is Kaiba thinking?

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:17.360
I flip over my set card!

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:19.160
Mask of Impregnability!

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:26.860
This Mask acts as a shield, protecting me from your attacks for one turn.

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:33.460
Blue-Eyes's attack didn't hit me.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.460
Too bad, Kaiba.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.950
I anticipated your attack!

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:42.970
You're lucky to survive.

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:43.950
What?

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:49.960
My Blue-Eyes could've attacked either one of you this turn.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:52.460
I could've attacked you.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:03.470
If I did, do you think your partner would've activated his spell card to protect you?

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:06.210
He definitely wouldn't have.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:10.710
Don't let him trick you!

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:15.620
I definitely would've activated my spell card to protect you!

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.850
Definitely!  Trust me!

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:19.850
I see.

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:23.700
Kaiba is trying to destroy their teamwork.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:31.560
Maybe Kaiba is right.

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:36.370
Mask of Darkness always bosses me around because he's bigger.

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:39.870
Dammit, Kaiba!  You didn't need to say that!

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:42.880
My turn!

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:52.120
When I was told that I could remove my bandages, I became more anxious.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:57.120
That's not good, especially since my brother was encouraging me.

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:00.940
Will you be ready to remove them for his duel?

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:04.630
Yes.  I think I'll have the courage when I meet my brother.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.130
Who would've thought he'd be such a good brother.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:13.640
He always gives me courage, so he's the most important person in the world for me.

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:18.140
I wish someone would say that about me!

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:21.740
Jonouchi, you're so lucky!

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:25.680
Jonouchi?

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.160
Jonouchi, you're okay!

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:32.770
C'mon!  Aren't you here to rescue me?

00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:34.660
Say something.

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:36.660
Jonouchi?

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.300
Jonouchi-

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:52.850
Pot of Greed.

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:58.250
The spell card Pot of Greed lets me draw two cards from my deck.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.250
This card is...

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:07.190
As long as Blue-Eyes is on his field, we're in a difficult situation.

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:10.730
I have to take a chance with this card.

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:13.860
First, I set a card.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:19.300
Then I activate the spell Card Exchange!

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:25.310
This spell card allows me to exchange my hand with someone else's.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:29.180
In a tag duel, I can exchange hands with my tag partner.

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:34.760
Since I have no cards in my hand, I'll just take yours.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.290
How selfish!

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:40.320
Hand 'em over.

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.970
Next, I activate the spell card that I set.

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:50.300
Chosen One!

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:52.870
Chosen One?

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:56.970
I place three cards in my hand facedown.

00:18:56.970 --> 00:19:00.800
One of them is a monster card.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:05.740
This masked top chooses one of the cards.

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:10.390
If it's a monster card, I can bring it out to the field.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.920
I see what you're doing.

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:15.630
I won't waste your hand.

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:19.130
If you fail to summon, I won't forgive you!

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:22.570
Here I go!  The masked top spins!

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:30.230
This method will allow him to summon a high Level monster in one turn.

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:34.920
Two of the three are spell cards.

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:40.450
But the one I want is the strongest monster card in our decks!

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:45.690
The masked top is stopping.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.630
The chosen card is...

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:58.900
Hooray!  Today is my lucky day!

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:11.830
Masked Beast Des Gardius!

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.390
Masked Beast Des Gardius!

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.070
3300 attack points?

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:24.220
It's stronger than Blue-Eyes!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.870
Nice!  You truly are the best partner!

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:32.020
You'll never lose if you trust me.

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:33.140
Understand?

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:41.700
His gamble also fixed their trust in each other.

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:45.740
Blue-Eyes is no match for Des Gardius.

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:48.280
What can I do?

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.440
I have one strategy left in my hand.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:57.400
But I can't do it if he attacks me.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:01.900
Which one should Des Gardius attack...

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:09.350
Should I attack Yugi and get rid of a player?

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:12.410
Or...

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:16.900
Should I destroy that annoying Blue-Eyes?

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:44.820
The Rare Hunters' counterattack have put Yugi and Kaiba in a pinch again!

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:50.250
What?  Kaiba is willing to sacrifice Blue-Eyes to let Yugi attack?

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:55.640
But Yugi says that he can't attack until Kaiba gives up his desire for revenge.

00:21:55.640 --> 00:22:01.280
To achieve true victory, will Kaiba use his trump card?

00:22:01.890 --> 00:22:04.750
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Obelisk the Tormentor

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:06.310
Duel, standby!

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:25.730
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:26.530 --> 00:22:31.100
I feel like I've been here

00:22:31.630 --> 00:22:40.760
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:41.070 --> 00:22:52.270
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:59.800
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:00.460 --> 00:23:05.070
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:05.630 --> 00:23:10.150
Will never change

00:23:10.840 --> 00:23:15.450
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:20.650
To be who I am

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:25.890
I've kept searching for something

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:30.570
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:33.530
I learned that's the answer

00:23:34.330 --> 00:23:40.640
From now until forever...
